I wrote a function to find the lowest unset bit in a u32. My friend says this optimized version is better but I'm not sure it's correct. Can you prove they're equivalent?

Original:
fn lowest_unset_bit_ori(x: u32) -> Option<u8> {
    let mut mask = 1;
    for i in 0..32 {
        if x & mask == 0 { return Some(i); }
        mask <<= 1;
    }
    None
}

Optimized:
fn lowest_unset_bit_opt(x: u32) -> Option<u8> {
    if x == std::u32::MAX { return None; }
    let y = x | (x + 1);
    let z = y ^ (y + 1);
    Some((z.trailing_zeros() % 32) as u8)
}

